            <ArticleTitle>[Superbrown beauty : The surface of tanorexia and tanning dependence].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>968-972</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00105-017-4052-y</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Brown skin symbolizes fitness, health, youthfulness and beauty, combined with leisure, activity, and joy of life in the Central European culture. Tanorexia is a tanning dependence that describes the morbid excessive desire for constant skin tanning. Particularly young women are affected. This article shows the underlying psychodermatological disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
